  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "The 2026 NCAA Men’s Basketball Tournament First Four, held March 17–18 at UD Arena in Dayton, Ohio, features matchups between the lowest-seeded automatic qualifiers and last at-large teams. The games include UMBC vs. Howard, Texas vs. NC State, Prairie View A&M vs. Lehigh, and Miami (Ohio) vs. SMU, broadcast on TruTV. Dates: Tuesday, March 17 & Wednesday, March 18, 2026. Location: UD Arena, Dayton, Ohio (hosting since 2011, except 2021). Purpose: To determine four teams that advance to the main 64-team bracket (first round). 2026 Matchups: UMBC vs. Howard, Texas vs. NC State, Prairie View A&M vs. Lehigh, and Miami (Ohio) vs. SMU. Broadcast: All games air on TruTV and can be streamed on March Madness Live, Sling TV, or HBO Max. The First Four allows the NCAA to expand the tournament to 68 teams, giving more at-large teams and conference winners a chance to participate.",
